  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 105 AM CDT Mon Jul 6 2026\n\nDry conditions are expected through Wednesday as an upper level \nridge over the Rockies should keep any convection from entering our \nCWA. The NBM has a slight chance of a stray thunderstorm Tuesday \nevening but have kept it as ghost POPs for now. Skies will be mostly \nclear through Tuesday with a slight increase in mid to upper level \nclouds Wednesday. Lee troughing across eastern Colorado will bring \nsouthelry winds to the area through at least Wednesday with some \nbreeziness across far western Kansas in the afternoon. As for \ntemperatures, lows this morning look to dip into the 60s with highs \nthis afternoon in the low 90s. Mid to upper 60s are expected for \nlows tonight with highs in the low to mid 90s tomorrow. Lows \nWednesday morning will dip into the upper 60s to low 70s with highs \nwednesday afternoon in the mid to upper 90s. Some areas along the \nKS/OK border may reach 100 degrees. \n\nThe upper level nigh gets pushed west thereafter with zonal west to \neast flow over the Central High Plains. Weak disturbances may move \nthrough this flow enhancing lift across western Kansas. The best \nchance of precipitation with these disturbances looks to be Thursday \nevening with lesser chances Wednesday and Friday evening/nights. \nTemperatures throughout this time frame look to reach into the 90s \nfor highs. Lows will generally be in the 60s with some 70s across \nsouth central Kansas.",
